1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,605
This is the House Move Agent: a multi-agent assistant, built on Neuro SAN, that helps a bank's mortgage customers tell everyone they're moving.

2
00:00:08,605 --> 00:00:12,095
On time, in the right order, and only with their approval.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,839
Moving home means telling fifteen to thirty organisations, and some of those are legal duties.

4
00:00:18,839 --> 00:00:21,883
Up to a thousand pounds for not telling the DVLA.

5
00:00:21,883 --> 00:00:24,555
Seventy pounds for not telling the council.

6
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:29,028
Sam Morgan's mortgage completion date has just been set.

7
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:31,254
Sam signs in to the House Move app.

8
00:00:31,254 --> 00:00:35,197
The sign-in, not the chat, decides whose record can be opened.

9
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:43,823
To watch the agents at work, we take Sam's signed session from the Account tab, and use it in nsflow, the Neuro SAN client.

10
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:52,088
Here is the agent network: fourteen LLM agents and twenty-seven coded tools, with the move coordinator at the centre.

11
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:56,488
Sam's session goes into SlyData, so every tool knows who is signed in.

12
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,161
Sam says: I'm moving house.

13
00:00:59,161 --> 00:01:00,204
Watch the graph.

14
00:01:00,204 --> 00:01:09,987
The coordinator asks the profile agent what the bank already knows, then hands over to the discovery agent, which reads ninety days of Sam's payments.

15
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:11,356
This part is sped up.

16
00:01:12,267 --> 00:01:15,865
Discovery finds who Sam pays, and what that implies.

17
00:01:15,865 --> 00:01:19,809
Pet insurance means a dog whose microchip needs updating.

18
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:24,583
There's a nursery, a car, a credit card, and the old mortgage lender.

19
00:01:24,583 --> 00:01:27,420
Anything uncertain is asked, not assumed.

20
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:36,389
The Internal Chat tab shows every hand-off: which agent called which, and each call to a coded tool, with its arguments and result.

21
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,706
Sam answers, and asks for the plan.

22
00:01:39,706 --> 00:01:45,824
The obligations agent applies twenty-five sourced rules, and looks up both councils live.

23
00:01:45,824 --> 00:01:49,605
The timeline agent dates every task in UK working days.

24
00:01:49,605 --> 00:01:55,448
Local services finds GPs, schools, and the water company, from Ofwat's official maps.

25
00:01:55,448 --> 00:02:00,741
Deadlines, fees and legal duties always come from code, never from the model.

26
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:06,514
The result is a dated plan, grouped by week, with the legal requirements marked.

27
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:08,488
Then the letters.

28
00:02:08,488 --> 00:02:18,381
Four specialist agents, for government, home and utilities, finance, and health and family, each decide which tasks are theirs, and how each should be done.

29
00:02:18,381 --> 00:02:25,104
The comms agent writes a letter for every task, with placeholders that code fills in only when it is sent.

30
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:33,060
Back in the app, the Move tab shows the whole journey, with Sam's place marked, and the next step: approve the letters.

31
00:02:33,977 --> 00:02:38,751
Sam can read every letter, then approve all the routine ones in one go.

32
00:02:38,751 --> 00:02:43,997
Legal requirements, like council tax and the DVLA, are approved one at a time.

33
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:45,809
Send them now.

34
00:02:45,809 --> 00:02:48,892
Complete emails go straight to the organisation.

35
00:02:48,892 --> 00:02:53,644
Anything the bank can't send itself becomes a pack, ready for Sam to send.

36
00:02:54,543 --> 00:02:55,627
Sam opens a pack.

37
00:02:55,627 --> 00:03:02,510
The letter is filled in, anything missing is highlighted, and there's a link to the organisation's own form.

38
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,995
Once it's gone, Sam taps: I've sent it.

39
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:15,155
Every step happens in the app, one screen at a time: the move overview with the whole journey, approving the letters, and sending each pre-filled pack yourself.

40
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:23,892
All of this is tested: a hundred and forty-eight unit tests, and live AI evaluations against ground truth for five customers.

41
00:03:23,892 --> 00:03:27,280
They even caught a real data leak, which is now fixed.

42
00:03:28,183 --> 00:03:29,662
The House Move Agent.

43
00:03:29,662 --> 00:03:30,366
Thank you.
